sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser
    participant DNS as DNS
    participant TCP as Transport
    participant TLS as TLS
    participant LB as Load balancer
    participant S as Server
    B->>DNS: resolve
    DNS-->>B: address
    B->>TCP: SYN, SYN-ACK, ACK
    Note over TCP: one round trip before a byte of your data moves
    B->>TLS: ClientHello
    TLS-->>B: keys agreed
    B->>LB: HTTP request
    LB->>S: to a healthy backend
    S-->>B: response, congestion window growing each round trip
    Note over B,S: latency is round trips, not bandwidth — that is why the edge matters
